Crop deferred accumulation snapshots to the stable scissor region.

gl-repl enables its accumulation-loop scissor on WebGL, where the code-panel
area can otherwise account for most of each canvas snapshot.  Record the
intersection of the LOAD scissor and framebuffer, lazily size RGB8 sample
textures to that rectangle, copy only those source pixels, and draw the
RETURN reduction through a matching viewport.  The materialized fallback
continues to preserve the original full accumulation texture semantics.

Also log the live deferred sampler capacity once, making browser verification
distinguish this path from the original immediate FBO implementation.

Performance measured 2026-08-24 under the same 1280x676, default-logo,
16x-accumulation-AA, 4x-canvas-MSAA run as the deferred-RETURN patch: two
interleaved 300-frame windows improved deferred full-canvas snapshots from
37.035 to 38.545 FPS (+4.08% incremental).  Mean callback interval fell
from 27.002 to 25.944 ms, saving another 1.058 ms per frame.  Together the
two deferred patches gained 13.49% and saved 3.500 ms versus accum-FBO.
See packaging/web/patches/README.md for the complete A/B.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after gl4es-accum-deferred-return.patch.
